        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): upgrade single newlines to paragraph breaks in post md messages",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #97074.\n\nWhen OpenClaw sends messages to Feishu via `msg_type: post` with `tag: md`, Feishu renders a single `\\n` as a space. This causes assistant responses with multiple paragraphs or structured lines to appear cramped and unreadable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`buildFeishuPostMessagePayload()` normalizes the markdown text before sending:\n\n- Single newlines outside fenced code blocks are upgraded to paragraph breaks (`\\n\\n`).\n- Existing blank lines are preserved (no double-processing).\n- Fenced code block internals are left untouched so code formatting is not corrupted.\n\nTo address ClawSweeper's review feedback, normalization now happens **before** Feishu's 4000-character chunk limit is measured:\n\n- Extracted `normalizeFeishuPostMarkdownNewlines` into `extensions/feishu/src/post-markdown.ts`.\n- Added `chunkTextForFeishuOutbound` so the outbound adapter chunks the already-normalized text.\n- Normalized plain text in `sendChunkedTextReply` before the reply-dispatcher chunker measures it.\n- `buildFeishuPostMessagePayload` still normalizes for edit and direct-send paths; the helper is idempotent, so double-normalization is safe.\n\nThis keeps the fix localized to the Feishu plugin while avoiding oversized post chunks after newline expansion.\n\n## User Impact\n\nFeishu channel users will see assistant responses with proper paragraph spacing instead of lines mashed into a single block, without delivery failures on newline-heavy messages near the 4000-character limit.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAdded regression coverage across the Feishu plugin:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run extensions/feishu/src/post-markdown.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/outbound.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/reply-dispatcher.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: 175 tests passed, including:\n- `post-markdown.test.ts`: 5 tests for newline upgrade, blank-line preservation, code-block preservation, no-op, and idempotence.\n- `send.test.ts`: existing + new regression tests for `buildFeishuPostMessagePayload`.\n- `outbound.test.ts`: 2 new tests for chunker normalization and 4000-char limit respect after normalization.\n- `reply-dispatcher.test.ts`: 1 new test verifying plain text replies are normalized before chunking.\n\nFormatting check on the changed files:\n\n```bash\n./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/feishu/src/post-markdown.ts extensions/feishu/src/post-markdown.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/send.ts extensions/feishu/src/send.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/outbound.ts extensions/feishu/src/outbound.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/reply-dispatcher.ts extensions/feishu/src/reply-dispatcher.test.ts\n```\n\nResult: all matched files use the correct format.\n\n> Note: full `pnpm exec oxlint` is currently blocked in this environment by a project-config/dependency reconciliation issue (`Rule 'no-array-fill-with-reference-type' not found in plugin 'unicorn'` / pnpm install timeout), but `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint --disable-unicorn-plugin` on the changed files reports 0 warnings and 0 errors.\n",
        "branch": "fix/97074-feishu-post-md-single-newline",
        "head_sha": "393e746d4dcff44e979cf9c4fba29ab64e05d5b7",
